Why Cloud Computing Matters in Cybersecurity

Cloud computing is important in cybersecurity because many organizations store data, run applications, and use computing resources in cloud environments.

Cybersecurity professionals need to understand cloud environments to help protect:

User accounts and identities
Sensitive data
Applications
Virtual machines
Networks
Cloud configurations

Moving infrastructure to the cloud does not remove security responsibility. Instead, it changes how security needs to be managed.





